# Local-only Cloud Functions configuration for the Firebase Emulator Suite.
# Copy this file to `.env` (gitignored - see repo root .gitignore) and fill
# in real values only if/when a given integration actually needs one.
#
# Firebase Functions (Gen 2) loads `.env` automatically for local emulation;
# see https://firebase.google.com/docs/functions/config-env for the
# project-specific variants (`.env.<project-id>`) used to differ config
# between tablecrew-dev/staging/prod once those projects exist.
#
# Scaffold note (Milestone F0): no real endpoints exist yet, so there is
# nothing to configure. This file exists now so the pattern - and the
# expectation that local secrets never get hand-pasted into source files -
# is established from the first commit, per docs/CI_CD.md's Secrets
# Management section and the "automated secret scanning" stage in
# .github/workflows/ci.yml's eventual stage additions.
#
# Real entries land here as each integration is built:
#   - Milestone F4 (Trust & Safety subset): none needed - reportUser/
#     blockUser/triggerDuressSignal are pure Firestore + FCM, no third-party
#     API key.
#   - Phase 1 (not Foundation scope): STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, PERSONA_API_KEY,
#     TYPESENSE_ADMIN_KEY - all real secrets, which per docs/CI_CD.md live
#     in Google Secret Manager for deployed environments, never in a
#     committed .env, and only ever in a gitignored local .env for
#     individual local development.
